---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Healthcare | BeaconGuard Authorization for Consequential AI Actions"
  description="BeaconGuard independently authorizes consequential AI-assisted healthcare actions before execution while preserving EHR, clinical, privacy, and operational authority."
>
  <section class="stack-section">
    <p class="section-label">HEALTHCARE</p>
    <h1>Authorize AI actions before they affect patients or operations</h1>
    <p class="lead">As healthcare AI moves from summarizing information to taking action, access alone is not enough. BeaconGuard checks the exact side effect before it reaches the system that will carry it out.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Consequential actions</h2>
    <div class="section-grid section-grid--compact">
      <div class="content-card"><h3>Patient communication</h3><p>Authorize the exact message or outreach action before it is sent.</p></div>
      <div class="content-card"><h3>Scheduling</h3><p>Authorize the exact create, change, or cancel action before scheduling state changes.</p></div>
      <div class="content-card"><h3>Operational record change</h3><p>Authorize the exact workflow or EHR-adjacent update before the system changes state.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>What BeaconGuard does not replace</h2>
    <p>The EHR, clinical judgment, privacy governance, patient-safety process, and healthcare system of record remain authoritative. BeaconGuard enforces the exact-action authorization boundary those authorities require.</p>
    <div class="page-actions"><a class="btn-primary" href="/design-partner-program">Evaluate a Healthcare Workflow</a><a class="btn-secondary" href="/trust-assurance">Review Assurance</a></div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
